The first turn of a session is lifted into `Conversation.system_message` (its text contents joined with "\n") and is not counted as a turn. This only happens when ALL of the following hold:
(a) `_hoist_leading_system_message` is True (it is for multi_turn);
(b) the endpoint metadata has `consumes_system_message: true`, which in v0.12.0 means chat, responses, messages and chat_embeddings, but not completions;
(c) `role == "system"`, `conversation.turns` is empty and `system_message` is None;
(d) `timestamp`, `delay`, `output_length` and `extra` are all None. Even `"delay": 0` blocks the hoist.
(e) there is no image, audio or video, and the joined text is non-empty.

The hoist is undone in two cases, and the system turn is then sent as a normal turn:
- the session has no other turns;
- the first remaining turn is also role=system.

The system message is re-sent on every turn:
- The worker passes `session.conversation.system_message` into every RequestInfo.
- `ChatEndpoint._format_messages` prepends {role: system, content: ...} unless the rendered messages already start with a system message.

During WARMUP only, `Worker._system_message_for_phase` returns "warmup\n" + persona, unless a cache-bust target is active. A conversation with no persona gets the plain system message "warmup". Warmup therefore never primes the persona prefix that profiling uses.
